> Multiplicity, lost order and a failed triangle inequality

The string aa has one occurrence of aa, while aaaa has three. Only one can
be consumed from the left, giving D=2/(1+3)=1/2 and J=1/3. Treating the
bigrams as sets would instead produce one. Conversely, abaca and acaba have
the same four bigrams, ab, ba, ac and ca, in different orders: their score is
one despite different strings. This is a feature collision, not a numerical
error. Literal case, spaces, punctuation and embedded NULs also remain part
of the input. Canonically equivalent UTF-8 spellings can have different byte
bigrams; neither character decoding nor normalization is performed here.

The dissimilarity d=1−D is symmetric and nonnegative but is not a metric.
Besides the equality collision, three tiny strings violate the triangle
inequality: ab and bc share no bigram, while each shares one of abc's two.
The following diagram's edge values come from actual scalar calls.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dice_nonmetric.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const double direct=1-dm::algorithms::dice_coefficient("ab","bc");
  const double left=1-dm::algorithms::dice_coefficient("ab","abc"),right=1-dm::algorithms::dice_coefficient("abc","bc");
  if(!(direct>left+right))return 1;
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(85,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=1.4;box.height=1;box.font_size=25;
  d.node("a",{0,0},"ab",box).node("b",{4,-3},"abc",box).node("c",{8,0},"bc",box)
   .edge("a","c",std::format("d = {:.6f}",direct)).edge("a","b",std::format("d = {:.6f}",left)).edge("b","c",std::format("d = {:.6f}",right))
   .text({4,1.8},"One minus Dice fails the triangle inequality",25)
   .text({4,-4.6},std::format("Direct {:.6f} > two-leg sum {:.6f}",direct,left+right),23)
   .save_svg("build/dice_nonmetric.svg");
  const std::vector<std::pair<std::string,std::string>> cases{{"aa","aaaa"},{"abaca","acaba"},{"",""},{"","a"},{"a","b"},{"a","a"},{"a","aa"},{"night","Night"},{"night","night "},{std::string("a\0a",3),std::string("a\0b",3)},{"\xc3\xa9","e\xcc\x81"}};
  const std::vector<std::string> labels{"repeat counts","lost order","both empty","empty vs one byte","different one-byte","same one-byte","one vs two bytes","literal case","trailing space","embedded NUL","UTF8 accent spellings"};
  std::print("| control | left bytes | right bytes | A | B | shared | Dice | Jaccard |\n| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t k=0;k<cases.size();++k) {
    const auto t=dm::algorithms::dice_coefficient_trace(cases[k].first,cases[k].second);const auto& s=t.overlap;
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} |\n",labels[k],t.left.size(),t.right.size(),s.left_bigrams,s.right_bigrams,s.shared,s.coefficient,s.jaccard);
  }
  const auto repeated=dm::algorithms::dice_coefficient_trace("aa","aaaa");
  std::print("\n| aa right offset | remaining before | remaining after | consumed |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");
  for(const auto& e:repeated.events)std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",e.right_offset,e.remaining_before,e.remaining_after,e.matched);
  std::print("\nTriangle control: direct {:.6f}; two-leg sum {:.6f}; violation {}.\n",direct,left+right,direct>left+right);
}
```
